1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,780
Microsoft's order backlog: 45% came from OpenAI alone

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,538
Microsoft sells Windows, Excel and cloud services

3
00:00:08,558 --> 00:00:12,411
Contracted future revenue was $625 billion

4
00:00:12,431 --> 00:00:16,357
If you own a US index ETF, you already own Microsoft

5
00:00:16,377 --> 00:00:20,761
OpenAI promised to buy $250 billion more cloud

6
00:00:20,781 --> 00:00:24,100
That's about 10x OpenAI's annual revenue

7
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:28,010
OpenAI has to earn more or raise money to pay it

8
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:32,246
Microsoft spends 60% of its cash on data centers first

9
00:00:32,266 --> 00:00:35,688
If OpenAI falls behind, only the buildings may remain

10
00:00:35,708 --> 00:00:40,144
Excluding OpenAI, orders still grew 25% in a year

11
00:00:40,164 --> 00:00:47,698
By Graham and Buffett's standards, fair value is about $376

12
00:00:47,718 --> 00:00:51,404
The current ~$525 is about 1.4x that

13
00:00:51,424 --> 00:00:55,424
If OpenAI grows as promised, this estimate is too low

14
00:00:55,444 --> 00:00:59,536
This earnings report, watch orders excluding OpenAI

15
00:00:59,556 --> 00:01:03,668
Will orders excluding OpenAI hold 25% again?

16
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:08,186
Want more like this? Subscribe and like
